<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Faidherbe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Louis Léon César Faidherbe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis Faidherbe was a French general and colonial governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> from 1854 to 1861 and 1863 to 1865. He pushed French rule inland along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a>, fought the Toucouleur Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">El Hadj Umar Tall</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor</a>, and founded the port of Dakar in 1857. He also created the Senegalese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirailleurs">Tirailleurs</a>. He later fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-faidherbe.jpg" alt="Louis Faidherbe" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie Madeleine Rignot-Dubaux · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Faidherbearmee.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
